  1→# live-verdict-screenshot-check - Test Specification v5
       2→
       3→## 1. Overview
       4→
       5→This test specification covers the live-verdict-screenshot-check sub-feature for the snake game, ensuring:
       6→1. Tests are not falsely marked as failed due to infrastructure timeouts
       7→2. E2E screenshots are included in PRs to prove game functionality
       8→
       9→## 2. Unit Test Coverage
      10→
      11→### 2.1 snake/internal/food Package
      12→
      13→| Test | Description | Expected Result |
      14→|------|-------------|-----------------|
      15→| `TestFoodGenerateNotOnSnake` | Food should not spawn on snake body | PASS - 100 iterations, no food on snake |
      16→| `TestFoodPosition` | Food position getter should return correct coords | PASS - position returned correctly |
      17→
      18→### 2.2 snake/internal/game Package
      19→
      20→| Test | Description | Expected Result |
      21→|------|-------------|-----------------|
      22→| `TestScoreIncrease` | Initial score should be 0 | PASS - score equals 0 |
      23→| `TestScoreIncreaseOnEatingFood` | Score should increase by 10 when eating food | PASS - score increases correctly |
      24→| `TestGameOverOnWallCollision` | Snake should trigger game over on wall collision | PASS - collision detected |
      25→| `TestNewGameInitialization` | New game should initialize all fields | PASS - score=0, gameOver=false, snake/food initialized |
      26→
      27→### 2.3 snake/internal/snake Package
      28→
      29→| Test | Description | Expected Result |
      30→|------|-------------|-----------------|
      31→| `TestSnakeMove` | Snake should move in set direction | PASS - head moves correctly |
      32→| `TestSnakeGrow` | Snake should grow when eating food | PASS - body length increases by 1 |
      33→| `TestSnakeReverseDirection` | Reverse direction should be blocked | PASS - reverse detected, 90° turns allowed |
      34→| `TestSnakeWallCollision` | Wall collision should be detected | PASS - collision detected |
      35→| `TestSnakeOccupies` | Occupies() should check body positions | PASS - correct occupancy detection |
      36→| `TestSnakeSelfCollision` | Self-collision should be detected | PASS - overlapping body detected |
      37→
      38→## 3. Build & Static Analysis
      39→
      40→| Check | Command | Expected Result |
      41→|-------|---------|-----------------|
      42→| Build | `go build ./...` | PASS - no errors |
      43→| Vet | `go vet ./...` | PASS - no warnings |
      44→| Race Detection | `go test -race ./...` | PASS - no data races |
      45→
      46→## 4. Integration / E2E Scenarios
      47→
      48→### 4.1 E2E Screenshot Script Validation
      49→
      50→| Check | Description | Expected Result |
      51→|-------|-------------|-----------------|
      52→| `e2e-screenshot.sh` exists | Script file should exist in `snake/scripts/` | PASS |
      53→| `asciinema.sh` exists | Alternative script should exist | PASS |
      54→| `screenshots/` directory | Screenshots directory should exist | PASS |
      55→
      56→### 4.2 E2E Screenshot Execution & Verification
      57→
      58→```bash
      59→# Run E2E screenshot script
      60→cd snake && ./scripts/e2e-screenshot.sh
      61→
      62→# Verify .cast file is non-empty AND has valid asciinema format
      63→test -s snake/screenshots/*.cast
      64→# AND first character should be '{' (JSON header)
      65→head -c 1 snake/screenshots/*.cast | grep -q '{'
      66→```
      67→
      68→| Check | Description | Expected Result |
      69→|-------|-------------|-----------------|
      70→| E2E script exits 0 | Script completes successfully | PASS |
      71→| `.cast` file created | File exists in `snake/screenshots/` | PASS |
      72→| `.cast` file non-empty | `test -s` returns true (size > 0) | PASS |
      73→| `.cast` file is asciinema format | First character is `{` (JSON header) | PASS |
      74→| `.cast` file git-tracked | `git ls-files snake/screenshots/*.cast` shows file | PASS |
      75→
      76→### 4.3 Git Tracking Verification
      77→
      78→```bash
      79→# Verify .cast files are tracked by git
      80→git ls-files snake/screenshots/*.cast
      81→
      82→# Expected output: list of .cast files including recent recording
      83→```
      84→
      85→## 5. Anti-Misjudgment Mechanisms
      86→
      87→| Mechanism | Purpose | Verification |
      88→|-----------|---------|--------------|
      89→| `-timeout 5m` on tests | Prevents default timeout misjudgment | PASS - explicit timeout set |
      90→| `-race` flag | Detects data races causing flaky failures | PASS - no races found |
      91→| `\|\| true` on timeout | Ensures script exits 0 when asciinema killed | PASS - exit 0 ensured |
      92→| Valid .cast format check | Ensures .cast file is asciinema, not empty typescript | PASS - JSON header validation |
      93→| Git tracking | Ensures E2E screenshots included in PR | PASS - files git-tracked |
      94→
      95→## 6. Environment & Setup Notes
      96→
      97→### Prerequisites
      98→- Go 1.x installed
      99→- **asciinema** installed (required for proper .cast format)
     100→  - macOS: `brew install asciinema`
     101→  - Linux: `pip install asciinema`
     102→- Terminal with color support
     103→
     104→### Running Tests
     105→
     106→```bash
     107→# Full test suite with race detection
     108→cd snake && go test -timeout 5m -race ./...
     109→
     110→# Build verification
     111→cd snake && go build ./...
     112→
     113→# Static analysis
     114→cd snake && go vet ./...
     115→
     116→# E2E screenshot (requires asciinema)
     117→cd snake && ./scripts/e2e-screenshot.sh
     118→
     119→# Verify git tracking
     120→git ls-files snake/screenshots/*.cast
     121→```
     122→
     123→## 7. Pass/Fail Criteria
     124→
     125→### All tests PASS when:
     126→1. `go build ./...` completes without errors
     127→2. `go vet ./...` completes without warnings
     128→3. `go test -timeout 5m -race ./...` all pass (12/12 tests)
     129→4. E2E scripts exist and are executable
     130→5. `screenshots/` directory exists with `.gitkeep`
     131→6. `.cast` file exists and is non-empty
     132→7. `.cast` file starts with `{` (valid asciinema JSON header)
     133→8. `.cast` file is git-tracked (visible in `git ls-files`)
     134→
     135→### Any test FAIL when:
     136→1. Build fails
     137→2. Vet reports issues
     138→3. Any test fails
     139→4. Race detector finds data races
     140→5. `.cast` file is empty or not in asciinema format
     141→6. `.cast` file is not git-tracked
     142→
     143→## 8. Test Execution Summary
     144→
     145→- **Total Unit Tests**: 12
     146→- **Build Checks**: 2 (build, vet)
     147→- **Race Detection**: 1
     148→- **E2E Scripts**: 2 (e2e-screenshot.sh, asciinema.sh)
     149→- **Git Tracking**: Verified for all .cast files
     150→
     151→All tests must PASS for this feature to be considered complete.
     152→
     153→## 9. Known Limitations
     154→
     155→### termbox-go in PTY
     156→- termbox-go may not initialize properly in all PTY environments
     157→- If termbox.Init() fails, the game will panic with terminal error
     158→- This is a known limitation and may cause E2E tests to fail in some environments
     159→
     160→### asciinema Python Bug
     161→- asciinema Python version 2.4.0 has a bug where it crashes with "ValueError: list.remove(x): x not in list" when terminated by timeout
     162→- The .cast file is still written correctly before the crash
     163→- stderr is suppressed in the script to avoid ugly traceback output
     164→
     165→### Headless CI
     166→- Cannot run snake game E2E tests in headless CI environments (requires TTY)
     167→- Unit tests can run in any environment
  
